  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Seychelles Federation of Workers&apos; Unions (SFWU) aims to develop and validate an innovative and inclusive strategic plan by December 2025.

To support the SFWU in developing and validating a strategic plan that positions the organization to effectively represent existing members, attract new groups of workers, and enhance the quality of services offered.

Participatory Needs Assessment:

Collaborate with the SFWU to conduct a participatory needs assessment involving:

In-depth consultations with SFWU leaders to identify key challenges and opportunities facing the union.
Surveys and focus groups with current and potential members to understand their evolving needs and expectations.
Analysis of the current operating environment, including labor market trends and emerging worker populations.
Strategic Plan Development:

Facilitate the development of a draft strategic plan with clear strategic directions and action plans. This plan will focus on:

Attracting new groups of workers: Identifying underserved worker populations and developing targeted outreach strategies.
Improving and innovating member services: Enhancing existing services or introducing new programs that better match the needs and preferences of current and potential members.
Strengthening advocacy and representation: Identifying key advocacy priorities and developing effective strategies to influence labor policies and regulations that protect and advance workers&apos; rights.
Stakeholder Consultation and Validation:

Engage SFWU members, employers&apos; organizations, government representatives, and other relevant stakeholders in consultations to gather feedback on the draft strategic plan. This will ensure alignment with the broader labor landscape in Seychelles.

Finalization and Validation:

Revise the strategic plan based on stakeholder feedback, and then facilitate formal validation by the SFWU leadership and membership.

By implementing this strategy, the SFWU aims to:

